WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.330
I wonder what it will be?

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.290
This week, it's this!

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.640
It's a Dark Signer card!

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.740
It's a Dark Tuner.  They can use it to 
Synchro Summon negative Level monsters.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.730
Hey!  Stop shaking!

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.590
Why don't you walk faster!

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:27.840
You're holding us up!

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.960
Many people with Markers are up ahead.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.850
Even Security doesn't dare 
enter this lawless area.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.740
It's like a district in Hell.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.740
I see.  It's a perfect hideout 
for people with Markers.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.930
Look over there.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.090
That's the Daedalus Bridge, 
the symbol of Satellite.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:57.220
It's also a dangerous area in Satellite 
named Barbaric Area After Damage.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.700
Also known as BAD.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.640
Looking over a vast distance

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.740
I realized my field of vision was narrow

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:30.650
Even if it’s easier to throw myself away

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:35.420
I want to survive to the best of my abilities

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.790
No matter how bad today is

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.770
There’s still the faintest light

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.170
All I have to do tomorrow

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.240
Is light it myself

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.240
I test myself so I won’t stop or vanish

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:05.210
Even if I get countless scars

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:11.510
I ride wishing for the 
arrival of a true tomorrow

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:15.490
Today will never exist again

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:21.390
So I won’t stop or vanish

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:51.280
Symbol of Freedom
Daedalus Bridge

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.160
No one's here.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.320
Are you sure this is where 
we're supposed to meet?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.910
Yeah, there's no mistake.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:07.320
Maybe Security captured Yusei and Crow!

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.360
You idiot!  Don't say that!  That's bad luck!

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.290
They're here!

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.980
Hey, Yusei!

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:24.140
Welcome back!

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.140
We were good!

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.400
Where are our presents?

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.750
What's wrong with you?  The moment you 
see me, you start asking for presents?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.350
I gave you presents this afternoon!

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.390
Don't be stingy!

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:36.370
Give us some!

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.380
Fine!

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.840
I don't have presents, but 
I brought the new King.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.280
The hero of Satellite, Yusei Fudo!

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.230
I know who you are!  You beat Jack!

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:50.010
Awesome!  It's really him!

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:52.060
It's the King!

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:57.670
C'mon kids, don't touch the King with 
your dirty hands.  That's bad luck.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.780
He's cool!

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.190
Give me your autograph!

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.420
Autograph!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.910
Where were those kids hiding?

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.720
They have no shame!

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.410
Maybe I should get Yusei's 
autograph while I still can.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.020
I might be able to sell it for a high price.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.490
Awesome!

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.690
How cool!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:19.440
You guys, don't break that D-Wheel.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:19.920
Yeah!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.190
We know!

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.440
Is that a true story, Yusei?

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:22.870
Here.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.170
Thank you.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.170
Yeah, I saw it.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.120
Satellite is destroyed in the future.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.140
You must be kidding.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:36.560
Does that mean Satellite is going to become 
the battlefield against the Dark Signers?

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:41.160
Wait a second.  Can you trust Godwin's story?

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.430
He's the one who put that 
Marker on your face, Yusei.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.590
I don't know if it's true.  However…

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.450
This and Stardust Dragon say 
that they're the enemies.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.900
Even if this place becomes the 
battlefield, I'll protect them.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.630
I'm the only one who can protect them.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.180
Yusei, I'll help you!

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.890
Crow, tell me that story!

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.250
That story again?

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.560
You love that story.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.160
So what?  I like Crow's stories.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.600
All right, I'll tell you the story.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:23.560
Long time ago, there was a small 
island that was very poor.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:28.080
The people who live on the island 
were not allowed to leave.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:32.620
All they could do was look at their 
neighboring island, which was large and rich.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.800
You're talking about City and Satellite.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.320
This story isn't a long time ago.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:40.730
Is that true?

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:45.780
Sheesh, you have to be "deliver" with girls.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.330
Don't you mean "delicate?"

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.150
Well, that's another way to say it.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.280
That's right.  This story 
is about City and Satellite.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:00.030
It's about a legendary man 
who tried to free Satellite.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:04.700
Long before you were 
born, there was a man who

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:08.050
always looked toward the City 
from this exact same spot.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:14.140
That man came here riding a D-Wheel 
that no one had seen before.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.860
Day after day, that man stood 
here and gazed at the City.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.280
But one day, he stopped doing that.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.420
Why?

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.290
That man discovered what he had to do.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:33.760
He discovered that he had to create the 
Daedalus Bridge in order to link with the City.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.930
So that means this bridge 
didn't always exist.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.860
But he didn't finish, right?  
That means it was pointless.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.070
It was an impossible task.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.440
That's what everyone thought at first.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.010
They made fun of him, calling him crazy.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.660
However, he never gave up.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:58.900
Even those that insulted him in the 
beginning began to think that he might succeed.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:03.900
Day after day, the only thing Satellite 
citizens did was recycle garbage from the City.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:10.480
They felt no hope until they saw the 
Daedalus Bridge as a bridge towards the future.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.000
It became the bridge of hope.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:19.710
However, there were people who 
didn't think this was good.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:25.450
They stopped construction and 
Security came to arrest him.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:29.520
Everyone gave up, realizing that 
it was impossible from the start.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.260
They would arrest the man 
and it would all be over.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.270
I'll never forgive Security!

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.380
Out of the way.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:37.460
Be quiet!

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.900
So what happened?

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:41.210
Uhh…

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.670
Security cornered the man.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.560
He had two choices.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:57.540
Either be captured by Security and live in

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.540
prison for the rest of his 
life… or live as a legend.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.850
The man chose to become a legend.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:29.070
Refusing to be tied down by 
logic or authority, he flew.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:39.550
From that day on, the D-Wheel became the

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:42.950
symbol of freedom ...and 
that man became a legend.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:50.360
Then what happened?  Was he okay?

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:53.540
No one knows what happened to him.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:55.530
However…

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:56.940
At the very least…

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.390
He lives in here!

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.580
Nice!

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.820
We also heard this story 
often when we were kids.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:09.200
Yeah, but I forgot about it.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.560
So that's why there are 
wings on your D-Wheel, Crow.

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.660
Be quiet!  I can do what I like!

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.220
Storytime is over.  Time for bed, kids.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.360
Go to sleep!

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.880
Good night, Crow.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.290
You should go to bed too!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.190
Be quiet!

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.070
Good night!

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:29.370
A man wanted to free Satellite 
and became a legend.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:33.770
I'm surprised there was someone like that 
in Satellite.  Yusei, that makes me think...

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:39.420
Your mark symbolizes that 
you're carrying on his spirit.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:46.780
I'm not like that.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.240
It's late.  We should also go to bed.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.300
You're right.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.530
Let's go to sleep.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.590
Good night.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.500
Good night, Yusei.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.290
This is today's news.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:10.780
A portion of the ancient Nazca lines 
suddenly vanished before tourists' eyes.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.890
Here's an eyewitness account.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:15.550
I was totally surprised.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:19.810
My wife and I were looking at the 
drawing on the ground from an airplane.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.390
All of a sudden, it started glowing!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:28.300
As I watched in shock, it vanished!

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.850
Then I said out loud...

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:34.210
"The Nazca lines are <i>history</i>!"

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:40.140
We've confirmed that pictures of a 
spider, giant and hummingbird have

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:45.140
vanished.  However, there are reports that 
other pictures have also disappeared.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:50.180
When the gates to the underworld open, those 
who'll lead the world into darkness will arrive.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:54.220
The Dark Signers have 
started to make their move.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:02.660
No one knows how gigantic 
pictures can suddenly vanish.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:08.140
It will take time to unravel 
this mystery scientifically.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:13.440
Jack, that picture was also on Ushio's arm.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:36.860
The first one has arrived.  Yusei Fudo.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:42.330
Much time has passed.  In 
order to atone for that

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:46.330
disgraceful battle 5000 years ago, 
you'll become our first sacrifice.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.140
He's my prey.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.510
Fine.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.000
I knew it.  You were planning 
to leave all alone.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:30.930
Crow.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.660
It's not nice to leave without telling us.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:38.470
This is my fight.  This has 
nothing to do with you.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.220
You never change.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.300
I don't want to draw you into this battle.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:49.460
Wait!  Are you saying that 
I won't be of any help?

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.590
You don't understand.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:55.420
You risk your life in a battle 
against the Dark Signers.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:13:00.150
It's different than a Riding Duel where 
all you care about is excitement.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:04.370
When you duel them, the 
battle takes away your life.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:08.310
You're actually risking your soul in battle.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:14.530
In the end, you may die.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:20.300
Since you're always serious, I know 
that you're telling the truth.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:25.780
However, I vowed to risk my 
life to protect the kids!

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:29.020
So you feel the same as me.

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.970
If you're coming, you know the risks.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:40.690
Don't underestimate me.  I'll be your guide!

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.540
The former Moment?  That's 
in the deepest part of BAD!

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.510
I know.  That's where they are!

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:57.970
You're striking straight into 
their heart.  Sounds like fun!

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.220
This way, Yusei!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.190
Yusei is missing!

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:06.740
Crow's D-Wheel is also missing.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.000
They left?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.280
Let's look for them!

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:11.100
Okay!

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:16.370
Saiga, you stay here in case they return!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:19.800
We'll split up and look for them.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:25.010
Is Crow gone?

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.510
Don't worry.  He'll come back soon.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.290
The fog rolled in.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.970
Come, Yusei.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.580
What's that?

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:06.400
That's right.  The war between the 
Signers and Dark Signers begins now!

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:15.060
What's this?

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:24.550
What?

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.900
Luca, what's going on?

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:32.340
Yusei…

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:38.160
I can sense it.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.270
Yusei, I know you're fighting.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.010
The vision that Crimson Dragon showed us…

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.660
Is something starting?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.760
Exactly what?

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:56.290
Yusei, what's happening to you?

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:01.560
Yeah yeah.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.020
It's the middle of the night!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.910
Can I talk to Master Atlas?

00:16:08.390 --> 00:16:10.330
It's me.  What do you want?

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:15.650
The Director ordered me to take 
you to Yusei Fudo immediately.

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.030
Please open the window.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.380
The window?

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:24.230
What's up with this?

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.340
I came to pick you up.

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:34.040
Hey, what's going on?

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.890
Yusei is battling against a Dark Signer.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.600
A Dark Signer?

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:45.450
How do you know that?  What's 
your relationship with Yusei?

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:48.160
That's none of your business.

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:50.760
Why?

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.090
Why are you also onboard?

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:56.400
What's your problem!  You came 
in the middle of the night and

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:59.400
interrupted my sleep!  The least 
you could do is let me tag along!

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:03.470
Non-essential personnel are forbidden!  What 
exactly is your relationship with Master Atlas?

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:09.400
Well, I'm Jack's so-and-so and we 
live together, so we're so-and-so…

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:11.310
That's enough.  Just stop talking!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.070
C'mon, listen to me.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:17.000
Anyway, I apologize for rudely 
visiting so late at night, King.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.950
I'm not the King!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.930
I'm sorry, Master Atlas!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:26.200
He's still aggravating as always.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.320
Wait a second.  The best 
way to handle Jack is...

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:34.920
When you think about it, 
Yusei shouldn't be the King.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:40.130
It isn't right for a no-name Satellite 
D-Wheeler to become the King.

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:44.750
Furthermore, he has a Marker.  How can 
someone like that become the new King?

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:48.400
You don't know anything about Yusei!

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.260
I hooked him!

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:53.070
He wasn't born in Satellite.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:56.560
Not only was he from the City, 
but he was born in the Tops!

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:57.670
Really?

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:04.270
His parents were researchers at MIDS, 
KaibaCorp's Moment Development Network.

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:07.800
They created the foundation 
of current Moment techniques.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:12.030
Wow!  I learned something incredible!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:17.770
But since he was sent to Satellite, 
does that mean he did something bad?

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:21.760
I know you've heard of Zero Reverse.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.730
Master Atlas, you're not 
allowed to talk about that.

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:29.970
If I remember correctly, it's an event 
that altered the landscape 17 years ago.

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:33.390
That's right.  City and Satellite 
was once connected, but that

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:37.390
event separated them into two, and 
that's how it's been to this day.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.800
There's a link between Zero 
Reverse and Yusei Fudo?

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:45.970
It wasn't a natural disaster.  
It was an accident.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:52.940
C'mon now.  That's not what 
it says in the textbooks.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:19:01.340
The current Moment's predecessor went 
out of control, causing the accident.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:05.970
The developers responsible 
were Yusei Fudo's parents.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:11.230
It was an accident?  That means 
everyone in the world was told a lie!

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:15.300
MIDS completely covered up the truth.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:20.610
Besides, a natural disaster was more 
believable than human-created powers.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:26.570
Yusei's parents lost their 
lives in the accident.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:31.170
Yusei, who was just born, 
was sent to an orphanage.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:35.310
If this story is true, 
then it's a huge scoop!

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.520
Go ahead and write the story, 
but no one will believe you.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:45.470
MIDS completely controls the 
information regarding this incident.

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:49.690
People believing you is the least of your 
concerns.  They'll most likely send you to Satellite.

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:52.030
I know.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.760
Safe…  My life was about to come to an end.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.340
He's here.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.110
What was that?

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.140
Be careful!  A Dark Signer is nearby.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:10.830
What?

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.800
Are you okay, Crow?

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:17.550
Yeah.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.770
Vorse Raider?

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:24.810
Yusei.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.000
And Crow is with you.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:34.780
You don't know how long I've 
been waiting for this moment.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.380
What?

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:37.970
How do you know our names?

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.370
So you've forgotten about me.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:48.470
No way!  Kiryu?

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:51.770
You're alive, Kyosuke Kiryu?

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:55.570
Yusei, thanks to you, I've seen hell.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:21:00.570
I'll get my revenge until 
you can't stand it anymore!

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:05.010
I don't know what you mean by hell, 
but this has to be a misunderstanding!

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:11.010
You're a Dark Signer?  You're 
going to destroy Satellite?

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:15.560
Find out how different I am than 
the person you used to know!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:30.820
Let's settle our destinies here!

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:34.540
This is the field where Signers 
and Dark Signers battle!

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.050
What?

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:38.660
What's this?

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:49.110
What's that?

00:21:51.390 --> 00:21:52.400
Duel!

00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:17.960
We look up and vow towards the shining light

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:23.030
We will build our own future

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:28.470
The far dawn shines blindingly

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:33.650
Awaken in the wonderland

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:48.790
The overflowing wave of emotions approaches

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:54.360
This world can’t be solved using algorithms

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:59.070
Even if it loses its light

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:04.340
The hourglass behind the 
heart can’t be turned

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:08.810
Roll the dice and get 
out and follow the light

00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:14.390
Fly towards tomorrow faster than a heartbeat

00:23:14.570 --> 00:23:19.250
This journey has no end

00:23:19.490 --> 00:23:24.730
There’s no meaning 
because there are no tears

00:23:25.160 --> 00:23:29.970
Hear my voice
